      "writtenOn": "2021-05-21T16:19:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m not sure where I got the 1ms timing from PS_RDY to the first SOP\u0027 message from the partner.  The timing shown on http://issuetracker.google.com/163478172#comment15 indicates that there was about 10ms from the PS_RDY to the EC mistakenly intercepting the SOP\u0027 message.\n\nIf there really is a PD partner that sends SOP\u0027 only 1ms after PS_RDY, we could still have a race condition where the EC hasn\u0027t disabled SOP\u0027 before the partner sends SOP\u0027.\n\nIt seems like it\u0027t better to leave the SOP\u0027 disable in the PE_VCS_Evaluate_Swap and PE_VCS_Send_Swap states. Was there a reason for moving this here, other than trying to consolidate the code?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 6311,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 6326,
        "endChar": 0
      },
      "revId": "a9b35e7e8590a0897c4f9a995f7447bf26c671b1",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "cc80aa23_0b270a74",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_pe_drp_sm.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 6326,
